.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1juybj/TASK-260715-1juybj_rework-02.md:5:- In the normative ownership sequence, move pending-capacity and already-stopped/generation-retired rejection to immediately after TCP accept and before SOCKS method negotiation. This branch closes the descriptor immediately, sends no SOCKS5 method reply and no RFC 1929 reply, and never hands the descriptor to authentication/adapter work.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1juybj/TASK-260715-1juybj_rework-02.md:10:Attach concise rework-02 evidence and route to `to-review`; do not self-accept.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1juybj/TASK-260715-1juybj_m0-capability-trace.md:37:| Bounded pre-admission | Caller injects a positive maximum pending count and `authenticationTimeoutMilliseconds`; pending descriptors are tracked in a bounded set. Current code applies that duration only as `SO_RCVTIMEO`, a per-receive inactivity bound that can restart with progress. It is not an absolute accept-to-authentication deadline, and authentication reply sends have no deadline. |
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1juybj/TASK-260715-1juybj_m0-capability-trace.md:38:| Lifecycle | Stop cancels the listener, shuts pending descriptors, awaits listener cancellation and authentication tasks, and is idempotent. Accepted rework moved listener close to its cancel handler and covered stop ordering. |
