### 1015 — Review: fork adapter-conformance seams accepted; three adapter-facing notes (TASK-260720-34d4du)
- MILESTONE: Fork extension accepted → `done`. Reviewer independently re-ran every gate: fork-tool exact-delta verify (20-file allowlist, archive/license SHA-256), 323 upstream XCTest + 13 fork Swift Testing cases, strict `swift-format lint --strict` on all 9 changed files, `make validate-core` (61 root tests, boundary check, build) — all exit 0. Attached patch artifact SHA-256 matches working tree (`b162e69a…88cf5c`).
- FINDING: External-signer coverage is complete for upstream's signature universe: `NIOSSHSignature.BackingSignature` has exactly ed25519/P256/P384/P521, and the fork's external-signature conversion (`UserAuthenticationMethod.swift:339`) covers all four. The `preconditionFailure` in the sync message init is unreachable from public API — the async `make` path is the only caller routing `.externalPublicKey`.
- FINDING: Snapshot lifecycle is sticky-correct: `SSHConnectionStateMachine`'s own snapshot resets to nil on transition to `userAuthentication`/`active`, but `NIOSSHHandler` re-reads it after every processed message while the KEX state machine still holds `NegotiationResult`, and only overwrites on non-nil (`NIOSSHHandler.swift:684`). Consequence: during a rekey the handler snapshot updates when the new `NegotiationResult` is computed (KEXINIT processing), slightly before newKeys activate.
- NOTE: Adapter caveats: (1) for AEAD ciphers (`aes*-gcm@openssh.com`) `macAlgorithm` reports the negotiated-but-unused MAC-list value — standard SSH semantics, do not treat it as the wire MAC; (2) `.global` promise resolves `.failure` as success-with-value (RTT measurable on refusal — correct for `keepalive@openssh.com` liveness), only connection errors fail the promise; (3) untested-but-documented paths: `.success` reply payload for `.global` requests and empty-allowlist fail-closed negotiation — acceptable residual risk, worth covering when the adapter integrates.

### 1003 — ReluxNIOSSH fork exposes adapter-conformance seams (TASK-260720-34d4du)
- IMPLEMENTATION: Public-key auth now accepts SSH wire-format public key bytes plus an event-loop future signer over NIOSSH's exact RFC 4252 payload; the offer stores no `NIOSSHPrivateKey`. Ed25519 and ECDSA raw signatures are converted inside the fork before the existing serializer and verifier paths.
- IMPLEMENTATION: Bounded generic global requests always set `want-reply`, use the existing protected packet queue, and resolve ordered success/failure replies. `keepalive@openssh.com` is proven by an explicit failure reply (valid liveness), with no TCP-forwarding listener or child channel.
- IMPLEMENTATION: Client KEX/host-key allowlists filter only bundled upstream implementations and fail closed when empty/unsupported. `NIOSSHHandler.negotiatedAlgorithmsSnapshot` copies exact KEX, host-key, cipher, and MAC strings from `NegotiationResult`; it never echoes configured lists.
- COMPATIBILITY: An initial pre-auth negotiated-algorithm user event caused upstream banner handlers that consume the first user event to stall. The event was removed; the immutable handler snapshot remains public and updates without injecting a new event into existing pipelines.
- VERIFICATION: The audited fork delta grows minimally from 16 to 20 files (four newly patched upstream paths, no new fork-only file). Exact-delta/license verification, 323 upstream XCTest cases, 13 fork Swift Testing cases, strict format lint, fork build, and `make validate-core` all pass.

### 0935 — ReluxNIOSSH adapter blocked by three missing public fork seams (TASK-260715-1af33i)
- BLOCKER: The neutral credential is an opaque async signer (`SSHPublicKeyCredential`), but ReluxNIOSSH public-key auth accepts only concrete `NIOSSHPrivateKey` and signs synchronously inside an internal message initializer. The adapter cannot authenticate without a candidate downcast/private-key export or a new external-signer fork API.
- BLOCKER: ReluxNIOSSH exposes only TCP-forwarding as a public global request. Its generic reply-requiring request sender and message type are internal, so the adapter cannot send/measure a supported `keepalive@openssh.com` request. Substituting remote TCP forwarding or writing encrypted packets beside the engine is invalid.
- BLOCKER: `SSHClientConfiguration` exposes transport-protection schemes but not caller KEX/host-key allowlists or a public exact negotiated KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC result; the only negotiation result/test accessor is internal. Inferring results from capabilities would violate E-ALGO.
- ROUTING: Product code stopped per TASK-260715-1af33i's explicit insufficient-fork rule. Recommended resume path is a focused TASK-260715-nzdzv3 fork extension for async external signing, generic/specific keepalive reply observation, configurable algorithm allowlists, and an immutable negotiated-algorithm snapshot/event. Full evidence and rejected forced fits are attached as `TASK-260715-1af33i_fork-api-blocker.md`.

### 0908 — Review: minimal ReluxNIOSSH fork accepted; two adapter-facing caveats (TASK-260715-nzdzv3)
- MILESTONE: Fork accepted → `done`. Reviewer independently re-ran every gate: `make validate-reluxniossh` (exact archive/license SHA-256, 16-file allowlist, 323 upstream XCTest + 10 Swift Testing, build), strict `swift format lint`, same-pin `conflict-test`, `make validate-core` (49 tests/build) — all exit 0. Default-path equivalence of the new adjust math to upstream verified analytically for even window sizes (default 1<<24); protected-byte boundary matches contract §10.1 (post-encode pre-write at `NIOSSHHandler.swift:266`, post-read pre-decode at `NIOSSHHandler.swift:205`); all outbound frames flow through the single `writeMessage` path.
- FINDING: During any KEX (client- or server-initiated) upstream's state machine rejects outbound `channelData` with `protocolViolation` (`SSHConnectionStateMachine.swift:1060-1076`), failing the child write promise. Pre-existing upstream behavior, unchanged by the fork — but automatic byte/time rekey makes the collision window likely under bulk traffic. The NIOSSH adapter (TASK-260715-1af33i) MUST gate/queue child writes on `rekeySnapshot.keyExchangeInProgress` / `NIOSSHRekeyStartedEvent`→`NIOSSHRekeySucceededEvent`; the fork exposes exactly this observability for the contract's "writes MAY suspend" clause.
- FINDING: `NIOSSHChannelWindowConfiguration` invariant is `remaining + buffered + delivered == initialWindowSize`, so remaining credit never grows past `initialWindowSize` even when `maximumWindowSize` is larger, and a `windowAdjustmentThreshold > initialWindowSize` (allowed by preconditions, which only check ≤ max) permanently withholds WINDOW_ADJUST — a stalled-channel footgun. Adapter policy must keep threshold ≤ initial (≤ half is sane). Cap semantics remain contract-correct: `remainingBefore + adjustment ≤ cap` always holds.
- NOTE: `.serverInitiated` rekey reason semantically means "remote-initiated" (a server-role handler labels client-triggered KEX the same way); cosmetic for the client-only tunnel. `requestRekey` in a non-active state fails the promise and also fires `errorCaught` — callers should not treat pre-active requests as recoverable no-ops.

### 0850 — Minimal ReluxNIOSSH window/rekey fork is reviewable (TASK-260715-nzdzv3)
- DECISION: The source fork is an independent SwiftPM package at `Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH`, based byte-for-byte on SwiftNIO SSH `0.14.1` / `31cdc3c` before a 16-file allowlisted delta. The `NIOSSH` product/module and upstream 16 MiB/no-auto-rekey defaults remain source-compatible; `ReluxTunnelCore` has no dependency on the fork.
- IMPLEMENTATION: Child initial window/cap/adjustment policy is set through a normal pre-open channel option and observed through snapshots/events; returned credit is earned only after pipeline delivery. Client manual, per-direction protected-byte, and injected-monotonic-time rekeys share the existing KEX state machine, coalesce concurrent reasons/promises, reset generation counters on success, and observe server-initiated KEX without product reflection or a test-only API.
- VERIFICATION: The audited archive SHA-256 (`0b135087…d06e6a`) and Apache-2.0 license SHA-256 (`cfc7749b…23d30`) reproduce. The full fork suite passes 323 upstream XCTest cases plus 10 deterministic Swift Testing cases; strict Swift format lint, fork debug build, 49 root tests, root build, exact-delta verification, and same-pin conflict preflight pass. The patch manifest, unified upstream diff, license/provenance review, rebase procedure, conflict command, and upstreaming split are task outcomes.

### 0821 — Candidate-neutral SSH conformance contract closes the shared-surface gap (TASK-260715-2ny6z4)
