 ### 0558 — Private HEV SOCKS admission and TCP byte ownership are frozen (TASK-260715-1juybj)
 - DECISION: The shared iOS/macOS HEV boundary remains IPv4 loopback plus a fresh per-generation RFC 1929 capability; loopback/TCP peer metadata is explicitly not process identity. A descriptor reaches `SSHProxyAdapter` only after capability proof and is positioned at the first CONNECT-request byte.
 - CORRECTION: Current `HEVSOCKSBoundary` uses `SO_RCVTIMEO`, which is a per-receive inactivity bound and can restart as bytes arrive; authentication sends have no deadline. The pending set is count-bounded, but current source does not prove an absolute accept-to-auth deadline. M1 must compute one monotonic deadline at accept, apply its remaining budget across greeting/auth reads, comparisons, and replies without progress extension, and prove slow-trickle/reply-stall eviction plus slot/descriptor release on iOS and macOS.
